{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":152483,"duration_api_ms":152434,"num_turns":4,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"af869530-c02f-4dd3-bdbd-93f3b1289806","total_cost_usd":0.4451498000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27406,"cache_read_input_tokens":114311,"output_tokens":2686,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27406,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":5,"outputTokens":2686,"cacheReadInputTokens":114311,"cacheCreationInputTokens":27406,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.295618,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":111,"outputTokens":7858,"cacheReadInputTokens":382583,"cacheCreationInputTokens":57498,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.14953180000000002,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"After reviewing the actual codebase, I agree with the planner's positions on all five amendments. The filter media scaling removal (fr-2-56410374) is incomplete without a parameterization path for seeded scenarios. The habitat-weighted shading suggestion (fr-2-7b7aa6d2) would double-count attenuation already encoded in the habitat light computations. The remaining three amendments correctly identify real issues: the test relaxation hides a regression rather than fixing it, and seeded scenarios lack explicit filter media area parameterization after the scaling removal.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-56410374","decision":"reject","rationale":"The working tree fix correctly identifies that volume-proportional scaling dilutes nitrifier density, but committing it as-is replaces one broken default with another. StartupOverrides has no filter_media_area field, ScenarioPreset has no filter hardware config, and FilterHardware::default() hard-codes 2000 cm². This means a 160L seeded tank and a 20L seeded tank would both get 2000 cm² of filter media — ecologically wrong in the opposite direction. The fix needs to be paired with an explicit parameterization mechanism (per amendment fr-2-c9744d27) before it can land."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-7b7aa6d2","decision":"reject","rationale":"Habitat-specific light attenuation is already implemented in the habitat computation functions: compute_glass_hardscape uses 0.3× crowding with column-average light at 0.4 base intensity, compute_substrate_surface uses 0.5× crowding with depth-attenuated light at 0.25 base intensity, and compute_plant_surfaces uses 0.3× crowding at 0.7 base intensity. The plant_shading factor in algae_growth.rs is a separate canopy effect representing overall light reduction from plant biomass above all surfaces. Adding habitat-weighting to this second shading layer would risk double-counting the crowding differentiation already encoded. No concrete failing test or calibration target demonstrates that glass biofilm is being artificially suppressed."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-b79c3c25","decision":"accept","rationale":"The working tree already reduced PLANT_BIOMASS_G_PER_1000_CM2_FOOTPRINT from 6.0 to 3.0 g/1000cm², which should substantially reduce self-shading. If plants still decline by 20% at this halved density under explicitly 'happy' conditions (good light, good nutrients), the self-shading model or another growth parameter is too aggressive and needs investigation — not a silently relaxed assertion. The constant should be validated against actual scenario footprints to confirm 3.0 is the right value before any test relaxation is considered."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-c9744d27","decision":"accept","rationale":"This correctly identifies the parameterization gap created by removing geometry scaling. With flow still scaling by volume but media area fixed at 2000 cm², seeded scenarios lose size-dependent biofilter/habitat differentiation. StartupOverrides lacks a media_area field, and ScenarioPreset has no filter hardware config section. Either the geometry scaling should be restored (perhaps with a corrected formula that doesn't dilute nitrifier density), or StartupOverrides/ScenarioPreset need an explicit media_area_cm2 parameter. This is the structural complement to rejecting fr-2-56410374."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-3782b77a","decision":"accept","rationale":"The test is named 'happy_plants_grow_with_light_and_nutrients' and its doc comment promises growth under good conditions. Changing the assertion to >= 80% survivability makes it a liveness check, not a growth check, while keeping the misleading name and comment. This silently removes an important end-to-end regression guard. If plants decline under explicitly favorable conditions, the root cause (overshoot in initial biomass density, aggressive self-shading model, or another parameter) should be fixed rather than accommodated by weakening the assertion."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"0c7bd757-0c5d-4157-89f7-943748e584bd"}
